leah: hi all, opened PR #467 to consolidate the tool-invocation and structured-output migration notes: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/467

tom: quick scan — looks good. two asks: 1) show how to handle positional args in examples, and 2) include a minimal JSON Schema users can copy into their validators.

raj: agree with tom. also we should include a tiny compatibility section for older SDKs that surfaced `function_call` instead of `tool`. sample sentence: "Map `function_call.name` -> `tool` and move `function_call.arguments` -> `args` (object/array)."

karen: our snippet-checker flagged one fenced block that had no closing backticks in the migration doc. failing line: ```js
const out = await client.generate(...);
console.log(out);
```

leah: thanks karen, fixed the fence and pushed. i'm adding two concrete snippets below so reviewers can copy/paste. please sanity-check.

---
JSON Schema (general tool invoke shape):```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "tool": { "type": "string" },
    "args": {
      "oneOf": [
        { "type": "object" },
        { "type": "array" }
      ]
    },
    "confidence": { "type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1 }
  },
  "required": ["tool", "args"],
  "additionalProperties": false
}
```

Python parsing pattern (pydantic example):```py
from pydantic import BaseModel, Field, ValidationError
import json

class ToolCall(BaseModel):
    tool: str
    args: object = Field(..., description='object or array')
    confidence: float | None = None

resp = client.generate(prompt=...)
payload = json.loads(resp.output)  # output contains the model's structured JSON string
try:
    call = ToolCall.parse_obj(payload)
    if call.tool == 'url_fetch':
        do_fetch(call.args)
except ValidationError as e:
    # fallback: try earlier shape (function_call)
    old = payload.get('function_call')
    if old:
        mapped = {'tool': old.get('name'), 'args': old.get('arguments')}
        call = ToolCall.parse_obj(mapped)
```

TypeScript quick parse (runtime-safe):```ts
const resp = await client.generate(...);
const parsed = JSON.parse(resp.output as string);
if (parsed.tool === 'url_fetch') { await fetch(parsed.args.url); }
```

raj: can we add an enumerated example for a common tool set? i pasted a compact schema for `url_fetch` + `db_lookup` that may help docs readers:```json
{
  "type":"object",
  "properties":{
    "tool":{"type":"string","enum":["url_fetch","db_lookup"]},
    "args":{
      "oneOf":[
        {"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"}},"required":["url"]},
        {"type":"array"}
      ]
    }
  },
  "required":["tool","args"]
}
```

karen: nit: add a callout that `confidence` is model-provided and not a calibrated probability. text suggestion: "Confidence is advisory only; validate against domain rules or your evals before automatic action." Also, include a link to the evals guide at /guides/evals/regression-detection.

leah: added the callout + link to PR. also replaced an old internal path in the migration guide that referenced `/sdk/python/old-tooling` with `/sdk/python/migration#tool-calls`.

karen: marketing asked for a redirect for the old path so external links don't 404. leah, can you open a tiny redirect PR to `_redirects.yml`?

